# Rewrites every top-level view route to the built React app's shell.
# Deliberately mirrors the exact former MainServlet @WebServlet route list —
# no broader, no narrower. Paths here are relative to the context root
# ("/jol" is already stripped by the time these rules run). No auth check
# happens here or anywhere server-side anymore: AuthGate (frontend/src/App.tsx)
# decides client-side, after the SPA loads, whether to show the login page
# or the authenticated app, backed by the existing SecurityFilter-protected
# GET /nav call.
#
# /react/*, /css/*, /fonts/*, /images/*, /sw.js (see web.xml's default-servlet
# mapping) and /jol/api/* (a separate Jersey servlet mapping entirely) are
# untouched by these rules on purpose.
#
# The bare context root ("/jol/") is deliberately NOT handled here — matching
# it needs a pattern like ^/?$ or ^$ against the empty-or-"/" relative path,
# and every such pattern tried threw a NullPointerException inside Tomcat's
# own RewriteValve (9.0.102) rather than simply not matching. See web.xml's
# welcome-file-list instead, which handles the context root through the
# normal servlet-spec mechanism without going near RewriteValve at all.

RewriteRule ^/(main\.jsp|main|lobby|deck|admin|tournament|tournamentAdmin|profile|active|login)$ /react/index.html [L]
RewriteRule ^/(game|help)(/.*)?$ /react/index.html [L]
